{"id":"lobbyist-giving-near-contacts","title":"Lobbyists’ reported contributions and the nearest reported contact with the same official","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"Since 2018 a lobbyist may not give to an official the lobbyist is registered to lobby. Where lobbyists’ own reports show both a contribution and a contact, how close together are they?","finding":"Lobbyists’ reports since January 2018 list 119 contributions tied to an official the same lobbyist reported contacting within a year. 24 of them (20.2%) are within 30 days of a contact and 4 within a week; moving each contribution a year earlier or later puts 11 within 30 days, so the two are closer together than the calendar alone gives. 16 of the 24 within 30 days went to a City-office campaign committee, the channel the ban covers; for 19 of the 24 the report names someone other than the lobbyist as the source of the money.","how":"This builds on the “lobby triangle” analysis, which pairs each contribution a lobbyist reported with that lobbyist’s reported contacts with the same official, by the names as the lobbyist typed them. Here each contribution is given the number of days to the nearest contact (negative: the contact came first), and the count within 30 days is compared with the same count after moving every contribution 364 days each way. The channel is read from the committee’s name, as in that script: a City-office campaign, a party-committee seat, a State office or a ballot-measure committee.","limits":"A lobbyist’s report may list a contribution the lobbyist delivered for someone else (the report names a separate source of funds), and the ban does not reach party-committee or State campaigns. Contacts are reported by month-end and can be entered with the wrong day. Lobbyists who report many contacts with one official are near a contact on almost any day, which is what the comparison measures.","columns":[{"k":"lobbyist","t":"Lobbyist","type":"person"},{"k":"firm","t":"Firm","type":"org"},{"k":"official","t":"Official","type":"person"},{"k":"given","t":"Contribution","type":"date"},{"k":"amount","t":"Amount","type":"usd"},{"k":"committee","t":"Committee","type":"text"},{"k":"contact","t":"Nearest contact","type":"date"},{"k":"days","t":"Days from contribution to contact","type":"days"},{"k":"channel","t":"Channel","type":"text"},{"k":"source","t":"Source of funds, as reported","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"lobbyist":"Piccini, Jacqueline","firm":"PLATINUM ADVISORS","firmKey":null,"official":"Peskin, Aaron","given":"2019-10-01","amount":500,"committee":"AARON PESKIN FOR SUPERVISOR 2020","contact":"2019-10-02","days":1,"channel":"City office campaign","source":"another person (not named)"},{"lobbyist":"Lazarus, Jim","firm":"San Francisco Chamber of Commerce","firmKey":"SAN FRANCISCO CHAMBER COMMERCE","official":"Stefani, Catherine","given":"2018-07-09","amount":250,"committee":"CATHERINE STEFANI FOR SUPERVISOR 2018","contact":"2018-07-13","days":4,"channel":"City office campaign","source":"another person (not named)"},{"lobbyist":"Piccini, Jacqueline","firm":"PLATINUM ADVISORS","firmKey":null,"official":"Peskin, Aaron","given":"2019-09-26","amount":500,"committee":"AARON PESKIN FOR SUPERVISOR 2020","contact":"2019-10-02","days":6,"channel":"City office campaign","source":"another person (not named)"},{"lobbyist":"GRUWELL, CHRIS S.","firm":"NEW DEAL ADVISERS","firmKey":null,"official":"Mandelman, Rafael","given":"2018-09-18","amount":500,"committee":"RAFAEL MANDELMAN FOR SUPERVISOR 2018 GENERAL","contact":"2018-09-25","days":7,"channel":"City office campaign","source":"another person (not named)"},{"lobbyist":"GRUWELL, CHRIS S.","firm":"NEW DEAL ADVISERS","firmKey":null,"official":"Walton, Shamann","given":"2020-02-22","amount":500,"committee":"SHAMANN WALTON FOR DEMOCRATIC CENTRAL COMMITTEE 2020","contact":"2020-02-13","days":-9,"channel":"party committee seat (no City limit applies)","source":"the lobbyist"},{"lobbyist":"GRUWELL, CHRIS S.","firm":"NEW DEAL ADVISE